  "finalResponse": "At commit `c9e8c2d`:\n\n- Canonical context: **1 MiB per file** (`1,048,576 bytes`).\n- Aggregate resume-read budget: **8 MiB** (`8,388,608 bytes`).\n- Always-loaded instruction budget: **32 KiB total** (`32,768 bytes`).\n\nSource, tests, and committed documentation agree on these boundaries. Exceeding either resource limit makes portable resume fail closed.\n\nStructural checkpoint validation is separate from freshness:\n\n- Structure requires every canonical section exactly once and in order, rejects unknown H2 sections, and ignores heading-like text inside fences, blockquotes, and CommonMark HTML blocks.\n- Passing that parser does **not** mean the checkpoint is current. Freshness is evaluated separately against Git state; a valid but stale checkpoint is reported as stale rather than treated as malformed.\n\nLocal checks actually run:\n\n- `format-check`: passed; 64 files checked.\n- `continuity-tests`: passed; 16/16 tests.\n- `git-diff`: exit 0; no changes.",
